From b0f904b4a0c49c504f7d82672251441d5dd9f8e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:55:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Blender relay: recognise another MCP server on port 9876,
 linear reply reader

The owner's 'Incomplete JSON response received' comes from the uvx
mcp-for-blender server when the bytes on 9876 never parse as one JSON
object. Blender Lab's official MCP add-on (same default port) does
exactly that: it ignores our unframed request, evicts the client after
10 s with an error object plus a NUL byte, and closes.

- ReplyReader: scans brace depth outside strings once per byte, parses
  once when the object closes; NUL or Blender Lab's words -> otherServer
  with a plain fix; clear messages for non-JSON and mid-reply closes.
- Heartbeat probe waits 15 s (past the 10 s eviction) and shows why the
  link is down in Last error; blender_status returns it as 'problem'.
- Tests: partial chunks (1..64 bytes), braces/quotes in strings, split
  UTF-8, 2 MB reply, size cap, NUL-terminated reply, end of stream.
- plans/mcp-bridge.md: troubleshooting section.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
